00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:27.000
to know, how do you feel about voter shaming?&nbsp;
I know that. You know a couple of things. Kyle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:35.040
and Mike Figueredo and a few other people.&nbsp;
I think Young Turks are generally against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.960
voter shaming, like, you know, criticized&nbsp;
from voters because they voted for Trump.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:47.940
But they'll sometimes criticize people who&nbsp;
voted for Trump because of the wall or because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:54.900
of, you know, the fact that he said banning banned&nbsp;
Muslims or, you know, Mexicans are rapists and all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.900 --> 00:01:01.860
that. How do you feel about voters? Do you think&nbsp;
it's productive? Do you think it's fair? Or do you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:08.040
think it's better to just stick to criticizing the&nbsp;
politicians? But, you know, because I basically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:12.360
I. I want to find out the best way.
Speaker 1: Okay. Yes. Right. So what? So so,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:16.560
listen, there's two things going on&nbsp;
here, all right? If you're asking me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:25.440
do y think it's inbounds, so to speak, for on&nbsp;
programs like mine, to be very frank and candid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:30.000
and direct about the fact that there is a lot&nbsp;
of dumb people in this country and many of them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.500
